From: =?UTF-8?q?Peijin=20Zhang=20=28=E5=BC=A0=E6=B2=9B=E9=94=A6=29?=
 <peijin@ustc.edu>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:21:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/32] Metal: w-layer inversion - three bugs fixed, one scale
 still open

The w-path now: spreads each visibility over support planes with ducc0's own
w-taps (TemplateKernel::eval2s: z = (z_off-nth)*2 + (W-1) with z_off the
distance in planes - i.e. the shader's poly_sample, NOT PolynomialKernel::eval,
whose argument is normalised to [-1,1]), and normalises the backward FFT by
4/grid^2 (ducc0's detail_fft::c2c is unnormalised, and the Hermitian half-plane
extraction accounts for 2 per axis).

Measured against ducc0's w-gridded inversion on identical data at w=0: with
those three fixed, the peak agrees to 2e-4 and the residual is ~1% rms - the
same order as the 2-D harness's reference-kernel caveat - but only after an
unexplained uniform factor 2.99. That factor is NOT a shape error (peak and sum
ratios agree), so it is one missing normalisation in the plane-sum path; it must
be understood rather than divided out, so -mgpu keeps using the verified 2-D
path and refuses where w matters.

Also adds bench/metal/wlayer_check.cpp + scripts/metal_wlayer_check.sh: the fast
bisection harness (seconds per run, pinned reference) that found these, plus
debug hooks MX_METAL_DEBUG_{PLANES,NOSCREEN,SCALE} for the next pass.

